# Acacia pycnantha Benth. (Golden Wattle — Australia's National Floral Emblem)
# Taxon concept, Fabaceae / Mimosoideae anatomical subsystems (PO:*),
# heteroblastic bipinnate-to-phyllode transition, pipe-model & biophysical allometry,
# InstanceState64 ontogenetic parameter bounds, ecological interactions (RO:*),
# and South-Eastern Australian Biocultural Country provenance (SPC / Local Contexts).
#
# Evidence boundary (per tree-cases.md):
# Taxonomic, morphological, and biophysical traits below represent sourced working
# reference bounds across the South-Eastern Australian dry sclerophyll forest,
# woodland, and heath range (SA, VIC, NSW, ACT). Exact site and individual
# occurrence remain pending.

