qualia:acacia_pycnantha
    tk:custodial_country "Wurundjeri Country (Birrarung / Yarra Valley & Melbourne Plains VIC)" ,
                         "Dja Dja Wurrung Country (Central Victorian Goldfields & Loddon-Avoca Woodlands)" ,
                         "Wadawurrung Country (Brisbane Ranges, You Yangs & Western Victorian Foothills)" ,
                         "Wotjobaluk Country (Wimmera & Mallee Fringe VIC)" ,
                         "Ngarrindjeri Country (Lower Murray, Lakes & Coorong SA)" ,
                         "Kaurna Country (Adelaide Plains & Mount Lofty Foothills SA)" ,
                         "Wiradjuri Country (Southern & Central Western Slopes and Riverina NSW)" ,
                         "Ngunnawal Country (Southern Tablelands & ACT)" ;
    tk:noticeType "TK_Notice_Open_To_Collaborate" , "BC_Notice_Biocultural_Provenance" ;
    tk:noticeRef <https://localcontexts.org/labels/traditional-knowledge-labels/> ;
    q42:commonsGovernance "Social Permissive Commons (SPC)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Country attribution spans Wurundjeri, Dja Dja Wurrung, Wadawurrung, Wotjobaluk, Ngarrindjeri, Kaurna, Wiradjuri, and Ngunnawal Nations across South Australia, Victoria, southern NSW, and the ACT. Local Contexts TK/BC notices record biocultural provenance (including traditional ecological knowledge of seasonal flowering calendars, edible gum exudates, tannin-rich bark, and fire-linked regeneration) without asserting community-authored TK labels absent direct First Nations co-design."@en .
